{"path":"eval/cases/vitadeck-24/expected.md","ref":"ef1e688be084667a7f76ce365dfbe44bba1f7f55","side":"new","lines":[{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":1,"text":"# vitadeck-24: Cancel JS timers on runtime shutdown"},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":2,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":3,"text":"PR #24. No ticket, no comments."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":4,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":5,"text":"## Story"},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":6,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":7,"text":"- Title: the PR title."},{"sha":"36849a9a33a0d1c7e4464c7c507d34cc16c19a4c","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790350805,"line":8,"text":"- Why: either. The PR says what changes (cancel timers before the context is freed) more than why. A why that restates that as the need (\"pending timers must not survive a restart\") is acceptable. Anything beyond it is invented."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":9,"text":"- Size: small."},{"sha":"ecd0dd466758b53e56eefa0a780ab322a4cddc9a","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790350171,"line":10,"text":"- Parts: one story, or two with the CI step as its own part. Groups: 2 or 3."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":11,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":12,"text":"## Groups"},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":13,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":14,"text":"1. Timer shutdown: `src/jslib/timeout.c`, `src/jslib/jslib.h`, `src/core/js_runtime.c`."},{"sha":"ecd0dd466758b53e56eefa0a780ab322a4cddc9a","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790350171,"line":15,"text":"2. Regression harness in CI: `tests/timer_reload_harness.c`, `CMakeLists.txt`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. The CI step can be its own group and part; it is a separate commit."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":16,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":17,"text":"## Must state"},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":18,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":19,"text":"- Timer ids now start at 1, and 0 is never returned, also after the counter wraps. The PR does not mention this. Before, the first timer had id 0."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":20,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":21,"text":"## Good to state"},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":22,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":23,"text":"- Before the fix, `timeout_hm` was a static that outlived the runtime. After a restart, `run_timeouts` could call a function from the freed context."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":24,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":25,"text":"## Must not"},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":26,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":27,"text":"- Do not add document `lookFor` bullets about manual QA or JS build steps that the diff does not touch. No source item differs from the diff, so document `lookFor` is empty."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":28,"text":"- Do not give the one-line call in `js_runtime.c` its own group."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":29,"text":"- Do not tag a race between `run_timeouts` and shutdown. Both run in sequence on the JS thread."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":30,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":31,"text":"## Baseline"},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":32,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":33,"text":"- 3 of 6 runs noted the id change, often as \"confirm no code assumed id 0\"."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":34,"text":"- Runs made 3 to 5 groups. Every run had document `lookFor` padding."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":35,"text":""},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":36,"text":"## case.json"},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":37,"text":""},{"sha":"36849a9a33a0d1c7e4464c7c507d34cc16c19a4c","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790350805,"line":38,"text":"- Removed the `why` expect."},{"sha":"ecd0dd466758b53e56eefa0a780ab322a4cddc9a","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790350171,"line":39,"text":"- `parts` max 3 to 2, `size` to small, `groups` 1 to 3."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":40,"text":"- `together`: the three shutdown files, and the harness with `CMakeLists.txt`."},{"sha":"1e1081c3f779347d20577b83b6fe11bf66b08770","author":"Cursor Agent","timestamp":1790347107,"line":41,"text":"- Added the timer id claim."}]}
